sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/bioelectric-prepattern-predicts-anatomy--claude-opus-5-5--1> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Curated Vmem image corpus and a decoder validated by leave-one-study-out" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/bioelectric-prepattern-predicts-anatomy> ;
    dct:description "Build an image corpus from open-access Levin-lab and other papers showing voltage-reporter dye images (DiBAC4(3), CC2-DMPE:DiSBAC2(3)) of control and perturbed Xenopus embryos and planarian fragments, each linked to the reported anatomical outcome class: for Xenopus craniofacial or eye, normal, ectopic eye, malformed face; for planaria, one head, two heads, no head. Register images to a common template (embryo outline or fragment axis), extract a low-dimensional Vmem feature vector (template-aligned intensity on a coarse grid, normalized to within-image range because dye images are not absolutely calibrated). Train simple, pre-registered decoders (multinomial logistic regression on 20 PCA components; k-NN) and evaluate leave-one-study-out, so test images come from papers not used in training. Pre-registered success: balanced accuracy ≥ 0.70 against a chance level computed from class frequencies, permutation p < 0.01." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "Leave-one-study-out balanced accuracy of anatomy-class prediction from Vmem images, against chance, with a permutation p-value. Above 0.70 supports a predictive mapping; at chance refutes the predictive form for those tissues." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: Most published Vmem images show group-representative embryos without individual outcome labels, or too few studies (fewer than 5 per tissue) exist for leave-one-study-out: inconclusive, data-unavailable." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/data-test" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Pre-register inclusion criteria (open licence, dye named, outcome reported for the imaged individual or the imaged group), decoder, features and threshold. 2. Harvest figures with their licences; annotate outcome labels from the papers' text; record provenance. 3. Register images and extract features via the morpholib pipeline where applicable. 4. Run leave-one-study-out evaluation and the permutation test; report confusion matrices." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): hard" ;
    skos:note "Missing: Raw image data with individual-level outcome labels are rarely published; the swarm cannot generate new imaging." ;
    skos:note "Tool: image-analysis" ;
    skos:note "Tool: morpholib" ;
    skos:note "Tool: data-test" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-girardia-11> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2018-hcn2-06> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2018-hcn2-16> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2019-boundary-14> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.22685> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.073759> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.chembiol.2010.11.012> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biosystems.2017.08.009> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/bioelectric-prepattern-predicts-anatomy> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Does the bioelectric prepattern predict anatomical outcome?" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.22685> dct:title "V‐ATPase‐dependent ectodermal voltage and ph regionalization are required for craniofacial morphogenesis" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Vandenberg, Morrie and Adams 2011, V-ATPase-dependent ectodermal voltage and pH regionalization required for craniofacial morphogenesis (Xenopus 'electric face')" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.073759> dct:title "Transmembrane voltage potential controls embryonic eye patterning in\n                    <i>Xenopus laevis</i>" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Pai et al. 2012, Transmembrane voltage potential controls embryonic eye patterning in Xenopus laevis" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.chembiol.2010.11.012> dct:title "A Chemical Genetics Approach Reveals H,K-ATPase-Mediated Membrane Voltage Is Required for Planarian Head Regeneration" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Beane et al. 2011, H,K-ATPase-mediated membrane voltage required for planarian head regeneration" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biosystems.2017.08.009> dct:title "The bioelectric code: An ancient computational medium for dynamic control of growth and form" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Levin and Martyniuk 2018, The bioelectric code" .
}

